---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CodeCard from '../components/CodeCard.astro';
import { ADDRESS_HISTORY_URL } from '../data/hosted';

const config = `[nest]
name = "rotki"
chain = "mainnet"
chain_id = 1
rpc_urls = ["https://your-ethereum-rpc"]

[address_history]
addresses = ["0xYourAccount"]   # rotki adds the rest of your accounts itself
poll_interval = "5m"

# optional: verified partitions instead of one RPC call per block
[address_history.mirror]
url = "${ADDRESS_HISTORY_URL}"
chain_id = 1
from_block = 17030000
to_block = 26159999
cache_mb = 2048`;

const run = `curl -fsSL https://nuthatch-indexer.com/install.sh | sh
nuthatch dev --dir rotki --trace-rpc https://your-trace-rpc`;

const check = `curl 'http://127.0.0.1:8288/api?module=account&action=txlist&address=0xYourAccount&startblock=0&endblock=99999999'`;

const parity: [string, string][] = [
  ['txlist', '2,318 transactions'],
  ['tokentx', '3,334 transfers'],
  ['tokennfttx', '106 transfers'],
  ['token1155tx', '53 transfers'],
  ['txlistinternal', '15 internal transactions'],
  ['txsBeaconWithdrawal', '3,131 withdrawals'],
  ['getblocknobytime', '20 of 20 timestamps'],
  ['nuthatchProducedBlocks', '8 blocks, rewards and MEV to the wei'],
];
---
<Layout
  path="/rotki"
  title="Nuthatch for rotki - Nuthatch"
  description="Run your own indexer for rotki: your accounts' transactions, transfers, withdrawals and MEV, served from your machine in the shapes rotki already reads."
>
  <section class="page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="section-label">rotki</p>
      <h1>Your accounts' history, from your own machine</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        rotki asks a block explorer for every transaction, transfer and withdrawal of every account you track,
        which means a third party learns all of your addresses. A rotki-mode nest answers the same questions locally.
        It watches only the accounts you give it, reads the chain over your own RPC, and serves the answers at
        <code>/api</code> in the shapes rotki already understands. rotki falls back to its next indexer for anything
        the nest has not fetched, so it never reads a gap as an empty history.
      </p>

      <div class="how">
        <div class="steps">
          <div>
            <span class="cap">1 · the nest</span>
            <p>One <code>nuthatch.toml</code> naming your chain, your RPC and an account. No contracts, no SQL, no Docker.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="cap">2 · the run</span>
            <p><code>nuthatch dev</code> backfills the accounts, then checks the chain every five minutes. A trace RPC is needed for internal transactions.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="cap">3 · rotki</span>
            <p>Under RPC Nodes, the Nuthatch nest tab takes the nest's address and puts it first in the indexer order. rotki registers your other accounts with the nest itself.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cards">
        <CodeCard code={config} lang="toml" label="rotki/nuthatch.toml" />
        <CodeCard code={run} lang="bash" label="shell" />
        <CodeCard code={check} lang="bash" label="check it" />
      </div>

      <section class="block">
        <h2>Checked against Etherscan</h2>
        <p>
          vitalik.eth on Ethereum, blocks 18,000,000 to 20,000,000, every row compared field by field with Etherscan's answer.
          Every count below matched exactly. Run end to end, rotki with Etherscan removed from its indexer order produced the
          same 557 transactions and 579 decoded events as rotki with Etherscan alone, and made no request to Etherscan.
        </p>
        <dl class="figures">
          {parity.map(([action, what]) => (
            <div><dt>{action}</dt><dd>{what}</dd></div>
          ))}
        </dl>
      </section>

      <div class="notes">
        <section>
          <h2>Light to run</h2>
          <p>
            The nest runs on its own small path, beside the indexer's event pipeline rather than inside it. On an M-series Mac
            it idled at 31.6 MB of memory, started in 179 ms and peaked at 45 MB during a backfill.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>What leaves your machine</h2>
          <p>
            Your RPC sees the queries it always would. The partition mirror, if you name one, sees your IP and the block ranges
            it serves, never an address. The MEV-Boost relays are asked only if you set <code>mev_relays = true</code>,
            because the block numbers they are asked about identify a validator.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>Partitions you can check</h2>
          <p>
            The hosted <a href="/nests/hosted/ethereum-address-history">Ethereum partitions</a> carry every header and
            withdrawal since Shanghai. Your nest hashes each header, links it to its parent, anchors the run to a finalized
            block from your own RPC and recomputes each withdrawals root, so a bad file is refused, never served.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem) clamp(4rem, 9vw, 6.5rem); }
  h1 { margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
  .lede {
    color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 2rem; max-width: 62ch;
  }
  code {
    background: var(--bg-inset); border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 0.05rem 0.35rem; font-size: 0.85em;
  }
  .how {
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg-elev); padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  .steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr)); gap: 1.2rem; }
  .steps p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
  .cap {
    display: block; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .cards { display: grid; gap: 1rem; min-width: 0; }
  .block { margin-top: 3rem; }
  .block h2, .notes h2 { font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.2vw, 1.35rem); margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .block p, .notes p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 1rem; max-width: 72ch; }
  .figures { margin: 1rem 0 0; display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; max-width: 40rem; }
  .figures div { display: flex; gap: 0.8rem; font-size: 0.86rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .figures dt {
    width: 13rem; flex-shrink: 0; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--text-faint); padding-top: 0.1rem;
  }
  .figures dd { margin: 0; color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .notes {
    margin-top: 3.5rem; display: grid; gap: 2rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(20rem, 100%), 1fr));
  }
</style>
